## Feature workflow (use the `ship-feature` skill)
1. A separate **test-designer** agent writes `{{SPEC_DIR}}/<feature>.md` and failing tests BEFORE implementation (it may only touch `{{SPEC_DIR}}/` and `{{TEST_DIR}}/`).
2. Implement until green without editing those tests; a needed change to one goes back to the designer, is made in its own `Test fix (designer): ...` commit and is explained in the PR. The spec lists the existing tests and scenarios the feature will break.
3. Push the feature branch (cut from `origin/{{MAIN}}`) and open a PR; a separate read-only **pr-reviewer** agent and the **browser-tester** (headless checklist, network stubbed; known failures are in `tools/browser-test/KNOWN-FAILURES.md`) run at the same time and their reports are posted on the PR.
4. {{OWNER}} reviews and merges. Agents may push **feature branches** and open **pull requests**; they never merge, never push `{{MAIN}}`, never force-push. Merging is what deploys.
5. No self-exemptions: small or UI-only changes follow the same steps (only {{OWNER}} can waive one, in chat). Details and the stand-in rule for unregistered agents are in the skill.

## Backlog (optional)
`docs/BACKLOG.md` is the priority-ordered list. When {{OWNER}} asks for "the next feature", take the first unticked, unblocked item, follow the workflow above, and say if the item is blocked and which one you took instead. Nothing starts on its own. An item is finished when {{OWNER}} has merged its PR.

